          <change when="2021-05-28T06:29:37-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/simoeis">Submit - In the context of a webinar on subliterary papyri taught in Summer Semester 2021 by me and H. Essler, I've entered this mathematical exercise. The text includes a new reading reported to me by J. Lougovaya: in IIb, l. 8, the correct reading for the fraction is certainly η ' (bis). The number is not executed very well and somewhat resembles a poorly written ζ, the interpretation of K.A. Worp. One-seventh, however, is not sought in any of the other operations and the (correct) amount recorded in the line, χκη, is that of one-eighth.</change>
